WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.710
- Fake talking cat, just
what we need around here.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.650
- [Narrator] Salem from
"Sabrina the Teenage Witch"

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.820
graced our screens in the '90s.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.160
- Salem, guard my door so
Jenny doesn't go anywhere, OK?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.760
- Hey, dogs guard.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.640
Cats watch and judge.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.370
- [Narrator] For the
actor behind the sass,

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.890
playing the role of a
puppet suited him just fine.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.510
- Puppets can get away with murder.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.333
Don't ever do a scene with
them, no one's looking at you.

00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:28.280
(cat meow)

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.113
Oh, ho ho.

00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:31.140
I'm having a bad fur day.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.050
Hi, I'm Nick Bakay, and I'm
best known probably as the voice

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.630
of Salem, the talking cat on
"Sabrina the Teenage Witch."

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:38.690
- Hit it, cat.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.560
♪ And I've got no defense ♪

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.760
- Salem was a very frustrated guy

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.540
who tried to take over the world.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.810
His punishment was they turned
him into a cat for 100 years.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.750
There was a lovely
bitterness to the character

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.400
that I leaned into hard.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.060
- Salem, you're the only
one who understands me.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.630
- Yeah, but it doesn't mean I care.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.430
- You know, I was in the
writer's room on that show too,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.070
so I could pitch my own jokes.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:02.980
- Maybe I should take your temperature.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.830
- Under the tongue, under the tongue.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.490
- Alright, I'll check in a few minutes.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.240
- [Nick] I was onset doing the
voice live first four years.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.470
Took a village to do that
cat because then you had

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.050
animal trainers and a
multitude of live cats.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.660
- Up and down and up.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.410
- And there was a remarkable
crew of puppeteers.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.700
Our head puppeteer was Tom
Founders who is really gifted.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.910
He ran the mouth and we had
Maury who moved the body,

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:34.190
and she spent her days in
darkness jammed into that kitchen

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.920
island counter, you know,
just working that body.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.860
It was a real team effort.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.780
- [Narrator] But Nick is
more than just a cat voice.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.670
- I was also the voice of Norbert.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.640
- Don't mess with the bull, my friend.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:46.960
You'll get the horns.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.931
- [Nick] The big older brother

00:01:48.931 --> 00:01:50.670
on the Nickelodeon
cartoon "Angry Beavers."

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.870
I've been a writer/producer
on a bunch of shows

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:53.940
like "King of Queens."

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.410
I also wrote the Paul
Barton Mall Cop movies

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.450
with my pal, Kevin James.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.919
- You're a nasty old man.

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:03.730
- [Narrator] And he's been
in front of the camera, too.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.606
On some well-known shows like Seinfeld.

00:02:06.606 --> 00:02:07.439
- No.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:08.272
- No, here.

00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:09.105
Just--

00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:09.938
- Please.

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:11.247
- [Narrator] That '70s Show.

00:02:11.247 --> 00:02:14.350
♪ I'm been cheating ♪

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.160
- [Narrator] And this AOL ad.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.158
- Thanks to America Online,
I'm really just goofing off.

00:02:20.158 --> 00:02:21.310
(laughing)

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.170
This is back during my
trying-to-make-my-career-

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.200
as-an-actor phase.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.520
You did some deep dig there, huh?

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.760
- So, it looks like it's just you and me.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.433
Wanna do each other's hair?

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:34.910
- I love cats.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.680
I've had cats my whole life.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.070
Up until very recently
we had a cat named Salem.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.560
A little black cat who
we rescued for 16 years.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.490
I tried to make friends with my namesake.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.210
It wasn't in the cards.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.353
Hated my guts.

00:02:50.286 --> 00:02:52.619
(laughing)

